<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n59309" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοσμ-ήτωρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ορος</span>,
			ὁ, poet. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοσμητής</span> (in late Prose, <i><span class="en">
			Jul.
			<u>Gal.</u>
			49
		</span></i> e), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who marshals an
				army, commander, leader</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀτρεΐδα . . δύω, κοσμήτορε λαῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.16
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				375
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοιὼ . . κοσμήτορε λαῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					3.236
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν χερσὶν ἔθηκε δέπας κοσμήτορι λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					18.152
				</span></i>
			; <i>guide, director</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παιδός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.194
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>one who adorns</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡρώων κ.
			Ὅμηρον</span> Epigr. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				76
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοσμητής</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				3.740
			</span></i>, al.</div>
